{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Who see the king's face.</b> There are places where the king does not appear to all his men, and in the Book of the Kings of Persia it is written that there are four ranks: the first-ranked princes sit first before the king, and this is the sense of \"who sit first in the kingdom\" — in the kingdom's rank."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:40.622609499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}